====2F====
There are two ladders inside [[Cliff Cave]], one leading up and the other down.

===Lower level===
The lower level emerges on a small beach. The eastern waterfall leads to the route's only patch of [[tall grass]]. The western waterfall leads to a clearing with a [[White Flute]]. Scale the rugged cliffs in the southwest with {{m|Rock Climb}} to find another cave.

====A Hiker's History Lesson====
A Hiker stands outside the entrance to the [[Embedded Tower]]. Speak to him to learn about the ruins hidden inside.

:''"Well, hello! It's said that past this hole used to be a huge tower reaching far into the sky. They say that it was a rather strange tower with half of it embedded in the cliff. It was not just a tall tower reaching up to the sky, but also reaching deep down underground! It is rumored that it even reached the bottom of the ocean! In short, the ruins used to connect {{p|Rayquaza|the sky}}, {{p|Groudon|the land}}, and {{p|Kyogre|the sea}} to each other... Most of the tower is now crumbled, and the only things that remain are the entrance and its interior, where you'll see strange patterns."''<!--
If spoken to again:
:''"I think this building may have been built to enshrine Pokémon with a strong connection to the sea, the land, and the sky."''-->

====Embedded Tower====
Strange patterns cover the floor, and mimic the markings on the [[super-ancient Pokémon]] found inside.

=====VS Kyogre{{sup/4|HG}}=====
With the [[Blue Orb]] in hand, {{p|Kyogre}} appears inside the tower. Its {{a|Drizzle}} Ability immediately summons a [[Rain|rainstorm]] that lasts for the entire battle, and boosts the power of {{type|Water}} attacks. {{m|Water Spout}} is a massively powerful move that grows weaker as Kyogre's health falls, but {{m|Aqua Ring}} allows it to restore its {{stat|HP}}. Begin with {{t|Grass}}- and {{type|Electric}} attacks to wear its health down quickly, then follow up with {{t|Fire}}-, Water-, {{t|Ice}}-, and {{type|Steel}} moves to chip away at it even further.

