=====VS Rayquaza=====
With the [[Jade Orb]] in hand, {{p|Rayquaza}} now appears inside the tower. Unlike {{p|Kyogre}} and {{p|Groudon}}, whose Abilities trigger adverse weather conditions, Rayquaza's {{a|Air Lock}} Ability negates any weather effects that may occur during battle. The legendary dragon excels in both physical {{stat|Attack}} and {{stat|Special Attack}}. Its strongest move, {{m|Outrage}}, causes it to rampage for several turns before becoming confused due to fatigue. Begin with {{t|Ice}}-, {{t|Dragon}}- and {{type|Rock}} attacks to wear its health down quickly, then follow up with {{t|Grass}}-, {{t|Fire}}-, {{t|Water}}-, {{t|Bug}}-, and {{type|Fighting}} moves to chip away at it even further.

